gridcoinresearch (5.5.2.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  The daemon's systemd units are new in this release. Existing service setups
  were switched over to them during this upgrade; this is what changed.

  The units are Type=notify: the core reports to systemd itself when it is
  ready, with no forking and no pid file. The units pass -nodaemon and
  -nodaemonwait, so daemon=1 or daemonwait=1 in a configuration file no longer
  matters.

  Autounlock moved to a socket-activated helper: gridcoin-autounlock.socket for
  the system service, gridcoin-autounlock@<user>.socket for a per-user core.
  The core asks the helper for the passphrase. Enabled autounlock setups were
  switched over automatically. No credential was decrypted, re-encrypted or moved: a
  per-user credential stays in /etc/credstore.encrypted, and the system
  service's /etc/gridcoin/wallet-passphrase.cred stays where it is, loaded
  through the drop-in
  /etc/systemd/system/gridcoin-autounlock.service.d/50-existing-credential.conf
  and owned by root, mode 0600.

  The old units gridcoinresearchd-autounlock.service and
  gridcoinresearchd-autounlock@.service and their RPC helper script are
  removed. They were disabled and stopped before the upgrade.

  The testnet package (gridcointestnetd) runs its system service as the account
  gridcointestnet.
  systemd hands the testnet datadir to the new account at its first start.

  A desktop user attaches the GUI to the system service through membership of
  the gridcoin-gui group ("Connect to the system service" in the menu). A new
  membership takes effect at the user's next login.

  A per-user core now needs "gridcoin-service enable-user <user>" before it
  starts: "systemctl enable gridcoinresearchd@<user>" alone gives an instance
  that stops with exit status 78 and says so. Instances that were enabled or
  running were set up during the upgrade, with the datadir they used, and
  running ones were restarted without waiting for them.

  Drop-ins of the old per-user unit (from "systemctl edit
  gridcoinresearchd@<user>") were renamed to
  <name>.disabled-by-gridcoin-switchover, so that their settings, written for a
  forking daemon, no longer apply. A -datadir set in one was kept. Review them
  and put back with "systemctl edit" what still applies.

  /etc/gridcoin/gridcoin.conf is created, if it is missing, as root:gridcoin
  0640 with generated RPC credentials. An existing one owned by root is given
  the group gridcoin and made readable by that group only.

  Ubuntu 22.04 builds have no autounlock (it needs systemd 251 or later): the
  old autounlock units were turned off there, and the cores start with the
  wallet locked.

  If the switch-over did not finish for a user, the upgrade said why, and
  /var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-main.state keeps what is left. Fix the
  cause and run "gridcoin-service switch-over
  --state=/var/lib/gridcoin-service/switchover-main.state". Until then that
  user's core is not restarted, and once stopped it may not start again.

  The full description is in doc/running-unattended.md.

 -- Gridcoin Developers <dev@gridcoin.us>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
